4|0@DotA2^1440672486#cuhbdav:ellran$:150 mana from boots = static amount dropping/picking up +int items = mana pool changing statically + percentage changing *relatively* example, you have 150/1000 mana. You have a soul ring and mana boots. Soul ring gives you a temporary +150 mana, which would be 15% of your total pool. If you drop the mana boots first, you receive +150/750 mana; which is 20% of your total pool. When you pick the mana boots back up; you'll have 35% of your mana pool compared to 30% if you didn't drop them; effectively giving you an extra 50 mana from the soul ring. The same concept applies to any +stat items, primarily str/int. The effectiveness just depends on the +/- differential.
