1|0@DotA2^1440678458#cuhdarq:ellran$:ok uhm 1000/1000 mana will change to 750/750 mana if you drop mana boots. It stays full (percentage) despite the numbers changing. This means if you have 150/750 mana it will take 600 mana to heal you to full. If you don't drop your mana boots it would take 850 mana to heal you to full. By reducing your HP/Mana pool it takes less actual regen to give you more hp/mp when you switch back. Base pools are affected by INT as well as simple mana boosts, so dropping other INT items also helps you to get more regeneration. The same applies to healing your HP. If you drop STR or +HP items before using the regen, then pick them back up, you get more hp regen. I hope that kinda helps more with less numbers.
